1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,488
Two servers in the same room, and they cannot talk.

2
00:00:03,508 --> 00:00:07,997
One typo in an address, a missing number after a slash, and nothing works.

3
00:00:08,017 --> 00:00:13,116
Every network problem starts with the same question: what is this machine's address?

4
00:00:13,586 --> 00:00:18,089
In this video: configure I P v four and I P v six addresses.

5
00:00:22,609 --> 00:00:25,192
Here's the task, the way an exam would state it.

6
00:00:25,662 --> 00:00:29,354
Configure IPv4 and IPv6 addresses.

7
00:00:29,824 --> 00:00:35,116
We'll look at the addresses, then give a new connection a static I P v four address

8
00:00:35,136 --> 00:00:38,572
and a static I P v six address, that survive a reboot.

9
00:00:46,092 --> 00:00:47,765
An address has two parts:

10
00:00:47,785 --> 00:00:51,759
the address itself, and after the slash, the prefix length.

11
00:00:51,779 --> 00:00:56,363
Slash twenty four means the first twenty four bits name the network.

12
00:00:56,383 --> 00:00:59,004
An I P v four address has four numbers.

13
00:00:59,024 --> 00:01:03,608
An I P v six address is longer, written in hexadecimal, with colons.

14
00:01:10,078 --> 00:01:14,976
On RHEL, Network Manager manages addresses, and the command is nmcli.

15
00:01:14,996 --> 00:01:17,827
A connection is a saved set of settings.

16
00:01:17,847 --> 00:01:22,317
A device is the network interface the connection is applied to.

17
00:01:22,337 --> 00:01:25,738
Settings saved in a connection survive a reboot.

18
00:01:33,208 --> 00:01:38,239
We will not touch the real interface, because that could cut our own connection.

19
00:01:38,259 --> 00:01:42,154
We create a virtual interface called dummy, made for practice.

20
00:01:42,174 --> 00:01:47,016
Before the demo, silently, the lab deletes any old connection named lab zero.

21
00:01:47,036 --> 00:01:48,847
This step changes the system.

22
00:01:57,367 --> 00:02:03,542
First, look. I P, dash b r, address. Dash b r means brief: one line per interface.

23
00:02:03,562 --> 00:02:10,115
Lo is the loopback interface, with the address one two seven dot zero dot zero dot one.

24
00:02:10,135 --> 00:02:14,648
Ens three is the real interface, with an I P v four address,

25
00:02:14,668 --> 00:02:16,462
and I P v six addresses.

26
00:02:26,982 --> 00:02:33,239
Now create a connection. Sudo nmcli connection add. Type dummy, a virtual interface.

27
00:02:33,259 --> 00:02:36,303
Ifname is the interface name, dummy zero.

28
00:02:36,323 --> 00:02:40,338
Con dash name is the name of the connection: lab zero.

29
00:02:49,858 --> 00:02:53,766
Now the addresses. Nmcli connection modify lab zero.

30
00:02:53,786 --> 00:02:59,582
I P v four dot method manual means: no D H C P, we set the address ourselves.

31
00:02:59,602 --> 00:03:03,811
I P v four dot addresses is the address with its prefix.

32
00:03:13,281 --> 00:03:18,573
The same for I P v six: method manual, and an address with slash sixty four.

33
00:03:25,043 --> 00:03:29,503
Nothing is applied yet. Connection up applies the connection to the device.

34
00:03:37,023 --> 00:03:39,964
Check. I P brief address show dummy zero:

35
00:03:39,984 --> 00:03:44,442
the I P v four address, and the I P v six address, both there.

36
00:03:44,462 --> 00:03:48,847
The last address, starting with f e eight zero, is automatic:

37
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:52,747
every I P v six interface gets one, called link local.

38
00:04:02,217 --> 00:04:05,681
And nmcli can show what is saved in the connection:

39
00:04:05,701 --> 00:04:07,936
method manual, and the addresses.

40
00:04:15,456 --> 00:04:18,892
Our five steps: task, demo, check, reboot, and your turn.

41
00:04:20,412 --> 00:04:23,472
We reboot. Dummy zero is back with both addresses.

42
00:04:23,492 --> 00:04:28,584
The settings were saved in the connection, so Network Manager applied them at boot.

43
00:04:37,104 --> 00:04:43,007
Your turn. Create a connection called exam zero, on a dummy interface called dummy one.

44
00:04:43,027 --> 00:04:47,568
Give it the I P v four address ten dot twenty dot thirty dot forty,

45
00:04:47,588 --> 00:04:48,794
slash twenty four.

46
00:04:48,814 --> 00:04:53,900
And the I P v six address f d zero zero, colon, twenty, colon colon, forty,

47
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:57,372
slash sixty four. Activate it, and run the checker.

48
00:05:06,842 --> 00:05:08,593
Try before you open the solution.

49
00:05:14,113 --> 00:05:16,717
Next up: configure hostname resolution.

50
00:05:17,187 --> 00:05:20,090
Subscribe to follow the series, and let's keep going.
